# An allowlist: everything is excluded, then the shipped files are named.
#
# The extension and the headless CLI ship as two esbuild bundles
# (out/bundle/extension.js and out/bundle/cli.js, scripts/bundle.js) with every
# dependency inlined, so the VSIX carries no node_modules and no tsc output.
# Adding a file the extension reads at run time means adding it here; the VSIX
# closure test (src/test/unit/repo/vsix-closure.test.ts) checks that every path
# package.json names is kept, and `npm run smoke:vsix` loads the packaged copy.
**
!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!PRIVACY.md
!SECURITY.md
# Top level only: media/screenshots/ is for the Marketplace README (served from GitHub).
!media/*
!docs/MANUAL.md
!out/bundle/*.js
!out/webview/*.js
# "MOAG: Install Command-Line Tool" copies these two out of the extension folder.
# moag-launch.js is plain Node (built-ins only), so tsc's own output is shipped.
!out/headless/moag-launch.js
!scripts/install-daemon-windows.ps1
